From 37b32cac92258cfef5704c6a2a5c42587d2f5039 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:45:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stack shape allocation as an operator control;
 sortable/filterable lineups

Skeleton allocation is one of the two real controls (6a/6b) and was reachable
only by hand-editing JSON. shape_allocation now takes relative weights per
stack shape (teammates-bringback); the operator sets the mix, the model still
chooses which game carries each shape. Zeroing a shape excludes it outright --
verified: NAKED goes from 3/40 to 0/40 with N_eff unchanged at 9.2, so shape
control costs no diversity.

- Skeleton.shape_key / shape_label, matching solver.classify() so requested
  and delivered mixes read identically
- build result reports the realised shape mix next to the requested one
- lineup table sorts on median/proj/ceiling/salary/ownership and filters by
  type and by contained player
